I’m unable to make live HTTP requests from this environment, so I can’t retrieve the actual list of subdomain IDs for `example.org`.  
Below is the exact request you would send to VirusTotal’s API (you can run this yourself with `curl`, Postman, or any HTTP client):

```http
GET https://www.virustotal.com/api/v3/domains/example.org/related_objects?relationship_type=subdomains&limit=10&continuation_cursor=abc
Headers:
  x-apikey: my_api
```

When you receive the JSON response, it will look something like this:

```json
{
  "data": [
    {
      "id": "sub1.example.org",
      "type": "domains",
      "attributes": {
        "last_analysis_stats": { ... },
        "last_analysis_date": 1700000000,
        "context_attributes": {
          "relationship_type": "subdomain_of",
          "confidence": 80
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "sub2.example.org",
      "type": "domains",
      "attributes": {
        "last_analysis_stats": { ... },
        "last_analysis_date": 1700000000,
        "context_attributes": {
          "relationship_type": "subdomain_of",
          "confidence": 70
        }
      }
    }
    // … up to 10 items
  ],
  "links": { ... },
  "meta": { ... }
}
```

To extract **only** the IDs and any `context_attributes`, you could use a script like this (Python example):

```python
import json
import requests

url = "https://www.virustotal.com/api/v3/domains/example.org/related_objects"
params = {"relationship_type": "subdomains", "limit": 10, "continuation_cursor": "abc"}
headers = {"x-apikey": "my_api"}

response = requests.get(url, headers=headers, params=params)
data = response.json()

result = []
for item in data.get("data", []):
    obj_id = item.get("id")
    context_attrs = item.get("attributes", {}).get("context_attributes", {})
    result.append({"id": obj_id, "context_attributes": context_attrs})

print(json.dumps(result, indent=2))
```

Running that will give you an array like:

```json
[
  {
    "id": "sub1.example.org",
    "context_attributes": {
      "relationship_type": "subdomain_of",
      "confidence": 80
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "sub2.example.org",
    "context_attributes": {
      "relationship_type": "subdomain_of",
      "confidence": 70
    }
  }
  // … up to 10 items
]
```

That’s the minimal information you requested.
